A wide church tower rises above the rooftops across autumn fields at dusk, its heavy bell swinging in the open belfry as the sound travels out over the quiet town of Fislisbach. In the foreground, green meadow grass falls away down the gentle slope into the wide valley floor, where scattered white and cream houses sit quietly among open patches of farmland under an overcast twilight sky. Along the far side of the valley, a wooded ridge displays orange and rust foliage of late autumn, framing the peaceful evening view across the valley. Ultra-wide view down across the meadow toward the distant church tower.

