Henri, an elderly man with short wavy white hair, a full white beard and mustache, soft facial lines, and small moles on his face, stands indoors beside the kitchen counter and holds a round wooden kitchen clock close to his face with both hands, squinting his eyes through level brows with his mouth closed in calm concentration. He wears a heavy brown wool cardigan over a cream collared shirt, grey wool trousers, and black leather shoes, with his bare forehead uncovered. Through the window beside the pale wooden counter, the evening lawn and scattered autumn maple leaves are visible in the dusk light. Close-up view showing Henri waist-up as he examines the clock face.

