Léa, a toddler girl with chin-length straight dark brown hair and eyebrow-length bangs, stands on the stone terrace step facing the garden, stamping one foot firmly down on the stone while clenching both hands into fists at her sides, her brown eyes wide, eyebrows pulled down tight, and mouth opened in a firm shout. She wears a long-sleeve red flannel pyjama top, matching red pyjama trousers, and thick red knitted wool socks. A few paces away on the wet lawn, Pic the hedgehog stands motionless beside a pile of red and gold maple leaves, gripping the pale pink-lined ear of the pale grey stuffed toy rabbit in his small mouth while looking back toward the terrace with round dark eyes and level brows. Medium view of the terrace step and autumn lawn at dusk.

